  },
  "front-cover": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "THE FRONT FACE IS A REMOVABLE COVER. The guide has a procedure for it (section 2.2.7): two thumbscrews release a bar that spans the front, with sixteen openings the breaker guards show through and the lamps, switch slots and card slot in its centre. It is drawn as the panel, not as a part, because the panel is never seen without it in service and the breakers, not the cover, are what a position holds. The slot under the lamps is the designation card holder the datasheet lists."
